# --ncu takes the launch from a measurement record: k5 at M=N=K=256 in
# blocks of 64 threads, the record's u32 parameters bound by position.
# Its text view: in the inner loop ptxas runs four address lines once per
# K iteration (32768 of <= 262144) and merges the eight ld.shared.u16
# lines into three loads; each epilogue st.global.u16 gains a PRMT.
RUN: %ptxroof analyze %fixtures/k5/k5.sm_89.ptx --ncu %fixtures/k5/k5.sm_89.256.ncu.json | FileCheck "%s"
CHECK: bindings: param 0 (param_0) = 256, param 1 (param_1) = 256, param 2 (param_2) = 256
CHECK: block size: 64 threads, 2 warps (64x1x1 from flag)
CHECK: measured (predicated-on thread instructions executed over the launch):
CHECK: <block 0>  consistent    10 instructions, 7 with SASS, 6 agreeing
CHECK: line 60: setp.eq.s32 %p1, %r8, 0;  predicted 1024, measured 2048  (ISETP.NE.AND x1, ULDC.64 x1)
CHECK: $L__BB0_3  consistent    111 instructions, 97 with SASS, 96 agreeing
CHECK: line 315: shl.b32 %r105, %r14, 3;  predicted <= 262144, measured 32768  (SHF.L.U32 x1)
CHECK: line 320: ld.shared.u16 %rs17, [%r110];  predicted <= 262144, measured 98304  (LDS.64 x2, LDS.U16 x1)
CHECK: $L__BB0_6  confirmed     412 instructions, 400 with SASS, 366 agreeing
CHECK: line 722: st.global.u16 [%rd52+10], %rs44;  predicted 1024, measured 2048  (PRMT x1, STG.E.U16 x1)
